-- title:
--   Analytic order at τ₀ is e times the order at a place
-- statement:
--   Fix $N \geq 1$ and let $A_N$ denote [`ModularCurve.LevelN.ring N`](def/ModularCurve_LevelNFunctionField.html#L28), the $\mathbb{C}$-subalgebra of the algebra of all functions $\mathbb{H} \to \mathbb{C}$ generated by the set consisting of the function `jAnalytic` together with all functions `fricke N v` for $v \colon \mathrm{Fin}\,2 \to \mathbb{Z}/N$ with $v \neq 0$ (in the packaging theorem invoked, such generators are pinned down by the formulas $E_4^3/\Delta$ and $-\tfrac{1}{2592}(E_4E_6/\Delta)\cdot(2\pi i)^{-2}\wp\big((v_0\tau+v_1)/N\big)$ for the lattice $\mathbb{Z}\tau+\mathbb{Z}$). Let $K$ be a field that is simultaneously a $\mathbb{C}$-algebra and an $A_N$-algebra, compatibly (scalar tower $\mathbb{C} \to A_N \to K$), and which is a fraction field of $A_N$; let $\tau_0 \in \mathbb{H}$. The assertion is that there exist a place $W$ of $K$ over $\mathbb{C}$ — that is, a valuation subring of $K$ containing the image of $\mathbb{C}$, different from all of $K$, and a principal ideal ring, with order function $\operatorname{ord}_W(f) = -\log$ of the adic valuation attached to its height-one prime — and a natural number $e > 0$, both independent of $F$, such that for every $F \colon \mathbb{H} \to \mathbb{C}$ lying in $A_N$ and not the zero function, the analytic order of vanishing at $\tau_0 \in \mathbb{C}$ of $F \circ \mathrm{ofComplex}$ is not $\top$, and its value as an integer equals $e \cdot \operatorname{ord}_W$ of the image of $F$ in $K$.
--
--   This compares the local analytic data of level-$N$ modular functions at a point of the upper half-plane with the valuation-theoretic data of the function field $\mathbb{C}(X(N))$: the order of vanishing at $\tau_0$ is a positive integer multiple of the normalised order at a place of $K$, the factor $e$ being classically the ramification index of $\mathbb{H} \to X(N)$ at $\tau_0$. It is used in the computations of the order of the $j$-generator at such places, namely [`ModularCurve.LevelN.exists_place_ord_jGen_eq_three_two_and_stabilizer_subset_zpowers`](thm.html#ModularCurve.LevelN.exists_place_ord_jGen_eq_three_two_and_stabilizer_subset_zpowers) and [`ModularCurve.LevelN.exists_place_ord_jGen_le_two_three_level`](thm.html#ModularCurve.LevelN.exists_place_ord_jGen_le_two_three_level).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_LevelN_exists_place_analyticOrderAt_eq_mul_ord.lean

